export const title = "RS485 (RS232)";
export const html = "<h1>RS485 (RS232)</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>When an application event occurs, you can send a message over an RS485 or RS232 interface. (RS232 isn't supported on some models.)</p>\n<p>RS485 and RS232 are configured the same way &mdash; only the output interface differs.</p>\n\n<h2>Basic Wiring Guide</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:640px;\">\n<div style=\"background:#2a2f3a;border-radius:10px;padding:20px 30px;color:#cfd6e6;font-size:11px;display:flex;justify-content:space-around;text-align:center;\">\n  <div>AUDIO<br>LINE IN<br>&#9679;<br>AUDIO<br>LINE OUT<br>&#9679;</div>\n  <div>LAN 1<br>&#9645;<br>LAN 2<br>&#9645;</div>\n  <div style=\"color:#f0c26b;\">RS-232<br>&#9645;<br>CAN<br>&#9645;</div>\n  <div style=\"color:#7fbf95;\">ALARM IN &nbsp; RELAY<br>&#9645;&#9645;&#9645;&#9645;&#9645;&#9645;<br>RS-485<br>&#9645;&#9645;&#9645;&#9645;</div>\n  <div>DC IN<br>9-36V</div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Rear view &mdash; RS-232 (DB-9) connector, and the ALARM IN / RELAY / RS-485 terminal block</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">RS-232 (DB-9) Connector Pinout</h3>\n<p>Below is the pinout of a typical 9-pin RS-232 connector, also called a DB-9 connector. A computer's COM port (DTE) is usually male, and peripheral devices connected to this port usually have a female connector (DCE).</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Pin</th><th>Signal</th><th>DTE Signal Direction</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td>1</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>&ndash;</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2</td><td>RXD</td><td>IN</td><td>Receive Data: Pin 2 (RXD) is connected to Pin 3 (TXD) of another device.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3</td><td>TXD</td><td>OUT</td><td>Transmit Data: Pin 3 (TXD) is connected to Pin 2 (RXD) of another device.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>&ndash;</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5</td><td>GND</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>Signal Ground: Pin 5 (GND) is commonly connected across all devices.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6&ndash;8</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>&ndash;</td></tr>\n<tr><td>9</td><td>&ndash;</td><td>I&ndash;</td><td>&ndash;</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">RS-485 Connector Pinout</h3>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Pin</th><th>Signal</th><th>Signal Direction</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td>1</td><td>TX+</td><td>Transmit Data+</td><td>Device A's TX+ is connected to Device B's RX+</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2</td><td>TX&ndash;</td><td>Transmit Data&ndash;</td><td>Device A's TX&ndash; is connected to Device B's RX&ndash;</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3</td><td>RX+</td><td>Receive Data+</td><td>Device A's RX+ is connected to Device B's TX+</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4</td><td>RX&ndash;</td><td>Receive Data&ndash;</td><td>Device A's RX&ndash; is connected to Device B's TX&ndash;</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">RS-485 Topologies</h3>\n<p><strong>Connecting RS485 4-wire to 4-wire (Full Duplex)</strong> &ndash; a standard 4-wire RS485-device-to-RS485-device configuration.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 220\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">MASTER</text>\n  <polygon points=\"60,40 100,55 60,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"65\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"10\">Tx</text>\n  <polygon points=\"60,90 100,105 60,120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" transform=\"rotate(180 80 105)\"/>\n  <text x=\"65\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"10\">Rx</text>\n  <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"700\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"700\" y2=\"105\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">120 &Omega;</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">120 &Omega;</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">120 &Omega;</text>\n  <text x=\"640\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5b6270\">120 &Omega;</text>\n  <g font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">\n    <text x=\"230\" y=\"30\">Slave 1</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"30\">Slave 2</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"30\">Slave n</text>\n  </g>\n  <polygon points=\"220,40 260,55 220,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"225\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"10\">Tx</text>\n  <polygon points=\"280,40 320,55 280,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" transform=\"rotate(180 300 55)\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"10\">Rx</text>\n  <polygon points=\"420,40 460,55 420,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"425\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"10\">Tx</text>\n  <polygon points=\"480,40 520,55 480,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" transform=\"rotate(180 500 55)\"/><text x=\"490\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"10\">Rx</text>\n  <polygon points=\"640,40 680,55 640,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"645\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"10\">Tx</text>\n  <polygon points=\"700,40 740,55 700,70\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23262f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" transform=\"rotate(180 720 55)\"/><text x=\"710\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"10\">Rx</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Connecting RS485 4-wire to 4-wire (Full Duplex)</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>Connecting RS485 4-wire to 2-wire (Half Duplex)</strong> &ndash; for 2-wire transmission, short the transmit (TXD) and receive (RXD) signals together on the RS-485 port. Wire the 2-wire device's send pin (TXD) to both TXD- and RXD-. Wire the device's receive pin (RXD) to both TXD+ and RXD+.</p>\n\n<h2>Action Settings</h2>\n<p>An RS485 or RS232 action can be added from the action settings screen.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>RS485</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Setting the action type to <strong>RS485</strong> reveals the related settings below it.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Message Type</h3>\n<p>The message type can be set to one of two formats: Hex Codes or UTF-8. Hex Codes is the default.</p>\n<p><strong>Hex Codes</strong> &ndash; lets you send binary data using hexadecimal values. Event metadata tokens can't be used when sending binary data; use fixed binary data instead. See the configuration example.</p>\n<p><strong>UTF-8</strong> &ndash; can be configured using tokens and a template. See the configuration example.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">RS485 (RS232) Setting</h3>\n<p>Configures Baudrate, Data Bits, Parity, Stop Bits, and so on. This setting is shared across every item of the same action type &mdash; so changing it from one specific action handler applies the change to every action handler of that type.</p>";
